<name>CVT</name>
<ttl id="1001Y_S000S_744HD_T007Y" variety="T007Y">
<name>CVT System [Super CVT-i] (K112/K112F)</name>
<para id="RM000000WGN00DX" category="C" type-id="800K5" name-id="32263-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>U0129/A2</dtccode>
<dtcname>Brake ECU Communication Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000WGN00DX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000047Q00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>CAN (Controller Area Network) is a multiplex communication system for vehicles. It is a serial data communication system for real-time applications, and has excellent communication speed and malfunction detection functions. By combining the CANH bus line and the CANL bus line, CAN performs communication based on differential voltage.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Malfunctions on the CAN bus (communication lines) can be inspected from the DLC3 connector. (Except for an open circuit in the DLC3 branch line)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Using TaSCAN, DTCs related to CAN communication can be checked.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>DLC3 is connected to the CAN communication lines, but CAN communication cannot detect malfunctions on the DLC3 branch line.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.14in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.86in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>1. Detection condition 2. Malfunction status 3. Malfunction duration 4. Other</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U0129/A2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Communication interruption between the engine control computer and skid control computer assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2.22 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>1 trip</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness and connector</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Skid Control Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>CAN Communication System</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000WGN00DX_02" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000WGN00DX_03" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000WGN00DX_03_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___000047S00000">
<scantool type="2"/>
<testtitle>Clear DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG ON and clear the DTCs following the TaSCAN screen display. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000FSM00TX"/>)</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Clearing the DTCs also clears the freeze frame data, so be sure to save the freeze frame data before clearing.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000WGN00DX_03_0005" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000WGN00DX_03_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___000047T00000">
<testtitle>Road Test</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a road test. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000FSU00TX_01_0005"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000WGN00DX_03_0001" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000WGN00DX_03_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000047R00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Read DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), following the screen display, display the [Diagnosis Menu/TCCS] screen and select [DTC Freeze Data]. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000FSM00TX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.65in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.48in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U0129/A2 is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U0129/A2 is not output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000WGN00DX_03_0003" fin="true">A</down>
<right ref="RM000000WGN00DX_03_0002" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000WGN00DX_03_0002">
